H3700.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to become pale, i.e. (by implication) to pine after; also to fear
KJV: (have) desire, be greedy, long, sore.

H3701.definition:
from H3700 (כָּסַף);
silver (from its pale color); by implication, money
KJV: money, price, silver(-ling).

H3702.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3701 (כֶּסֶף)
{silver (from its pale color); by implication, money}
KJV: money, silver.

H3703.definition:
perhaps from H3701 (כֶּסֶף); silvery;
Casiphja, a place in Babylon
KJV: Casiphia.

H3704.definition:
from H3680 (כָּסָה);
a cushion or pillow (as covering a seat or bed)
KJV: pillow.

H3705.definition:
(Aramaic) probably from H3652 (כֵּן);
now
KJV: now.

H3706.definition:
(Aramaic) or כְּעֶת; (Aramaic), feminine of H3705 (כְּעַן);
thus (only in the formula 'and so forth')
KJV: at such a time.

H3707.definition:
a primitive root;
to trouble; by implication, to grieve, rage, be indignant
KJV: be angry, be grieved, take indignation, provoke (to anger, unto wrath), have sorrow, vex, be wroth.

H3708.definition:
or (in Job) כַּעַשׂ; from H3707 (כַּעַס);
vexation
KJV: anger, angry, grief, indignation, provocation, provoking, [idiom] sore, sorrow, spite, wrath.

H3709.definition:
from H3721 (כָּפַף);
the hollow hand or palm (so of the paw of an animal, of the sole, and even of the bowl of a dish or sling, the handle of a bolt, the leaves of a palm-tree); figuratively, power
KJV: branch, [phrase] foot, hand((-ful), -dle, (-led)), hollow, middle, palm, paw, power, sole, spoon.

H3710.definition:
from H3721 (כָּפַף);
a hollow rock
KJV: rock.

H3711.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to bend, i.e. (figuratively) to tame or subdue
KJV: pacify.

H3712.definition:
feminine of H3709 (כַּף);
a leaf of a palmtree
KJV: branch.

H3713.definition:
from H3722 (כָּפַר);
properly, a cover, i.e. (by implication) a tankard (or covered goblet); also white frost (as covering the ground)
KJV: bason, hoar(-y) frost.

H3714.definition:
from an unused root meaning to connect;
a girder
KJV: beam.

H3715.definition:
from H3722 (כָּפַר);
a village (as covered in by walls); also a young lion (perhaps as covered with a mane)
KJV: (young) lion, village. Compare H3723 (כָּפָר).

H3716.definition:
feminine of H3715 (כְּפִיר); the village (always with the art.);
Kephirah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Chephirah.

H3717.definition:
a primitive root;
to fold together; figuratively, to repeat
KJV: double.

H3718.definition:
from H3717 (כָּפַל);
a duplicate
KJV: double.

H3719.definition:
a primitive root;
to bend
KJV: bend.

H3720.definition:
from H3719 (כָּפַן);
hunger (as making to stoop with emptiness and pain)
KJV: famine.

H3721.definition:
a primitive root;
to curve
KJV: bow down (self).

H3722.definition:
a primitive root;
to cover (specifically with bitumen); figuratively, to expiate or condone, to placate or cancel
KJV: appease, make (an atonement, cleanse, disannul, forgive, be merciful, pacify, pardon, purge (away), put off, (make) reconcile(-liation).

H3723.definition:
from H3722 (כָּפַר);
a village (as protected by walls)
KJV: village. Compare H3715 (כְּפִיר).

H3724.definition:
from H3722 (כָּפַר);
properly, a cover, i.e. (literally) a village (as covered in); (specifically) bitumen (as used for coating), and the henna plant (as used for dyeing); figuratively, a redemption-price
KJV: bribe, camphire, pitch, ransom, satisfaction, sum of money, village.

H3725.definition:
from H3722 (כָּפַר);
expiation (only in plural)
KJV: atonement.

H3726.definition:
from H3723 (כָּפָר) and H5984 (עַמּוֹנִי), with the article interposed; village of the Ammonite;
Kefar-ha-Ammoni, a place in Palestine
KJV: Chefarhaamonai.

H3727.definition:
from H3722 (כָּפַר);
a lid (used only of the cover of the sacred Ark)
KJV: mercy seat.

H3728.definition:
a primitive root;
to tread down; figuratively, to humiliate
KJV: cover.

H3729.definition:
(Aramaic) a root of uncertain correspondence;
to fetter
KJV: bind.

H3730.definition:
or (Amos 9:1) כַּפְתּוֹר; probably from an unused root meaning to encircle;
a chaplet; but used only in an architectonic sense, i.e. the capital of acolumn, or a wreath-like button or disk on the candelabrum
KJV: knop, (upper) lintel.

H3731.definition:
or (Amos 9:7) כַּפְתּוֹר; apparently the same as H3730 (כַּפְתֹּר);
Caphtor (i.e. a wreath-shaped island), the original seat of the Philistines
KJV: Caphtor.

H3732.definition:
patrial from H3731 (כַּפְתֹּר);
a Caphtorite (collectively) or native of Caphtor
KJV: Caphthorim, Caphtorim(-s).

H3733.definition:
from H3769 (כָּרַר) in the sense of plumpness;
a ram (as full-grown and fat), including a battering-ram (as butting); hence, a meadow (as for sheep); also a pad or camel's saddle (as puffed out)
KJV: captain, furniture, lamb, (large) pasture, ram. See also H1033 (בֵּית כַּר), H3746 (כָּרִי).

H3734.definition:
from the same as H3564 (כּוּר);
properly, a deep round vessel, i.e. (specifically) a cor or measure for things dry
KJV: cor, measure. Aramaic the same.

H3735.definition:
(Aramaic) probably corresponding to H3738 (כָּרָה) in the sense of piercing(figuratively);
to grieve
KJV: be grieved.

H3736.definition:
from the same as H3525 (כֶּבֶל);
to gird or clothe
KJV: clothed.

H3737.definition:
(Aramaic) from a verb corresponding to that of H3736 (כַּרְבֵּל);
a mantle
KJV: hat.

H3738.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to dig; figuratively, to plot; generally, to bore or open
KJV: dig, [idiom] make (a banquet), open.

H3739.definition:
usually assigned as a primitive root, but probably only a special application of H3738 (כָּרָה) (through the common idea of planning implied in a bargain);
to purchase
KJV: buy, prepare.

H3740.definition:
from H3739 (כָּרָה);
a purchase
KJV: provision.

H3741.definition:
feminine of H3733 (כַּר);
a meadow
KJV: cottage.

H3742.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
a cherub or imaginary figure
KJV: cherub, (plural) cherubims.

H3743.definition:
the same as H3742 (כְּרוּב);
Kerub, a place in Babylon
KJV: Cherub.

H3744.definition:
(Aramaic) from H3745 (כְּרַז);
a herald
KJV: herald.

H3745.definition:
(Aramaic) probably of Greek origin;
to proclaim
KJV: make a proclamation.

H3746.definition:
perhaps an abridged plural of H3733 (כַּר) in the sense of leader (of the flock);
a life-guardsman
KJV: captains, Cherethites (from the margin).

H3747.definition:
from H3772 (כָּרַת); a cut;
Kerith, a brook of Palestine
KJV: Cherith.

H3748.definition:
from H3772 (כָּרַת);
a cutting (of the matrimonial bond), i.e. divorce
KJV: divorce(-ment).

H3749.definition:
expanded from the same as H3522 (כַּבּוֹן);
a rim or top margin
KJV: compass.

H3750.definition:
probably of foreign origin;
the crocus
KJV: saffron.

H3751.definition:
of foreign derivation;
Karkemish, a place in Syria
KJV: Carchemish.

H3752.definition:
of Persian origin;
Karkas, a eunuch of Xerxes
KJV: Carcas.

H3753.definition:
from H3769 (כָּרַר);
a dromedary (from its rapid motion as if dancing)
KJV: swift beast.

H3754.definition:
from an unused root of uncertain meaning;
a garden or vineyard
KJV: vines, (increase of the) vineyard(-s), vintage. See also H1021 (בֵּית הַכֶּרֶם).

H3755.definition:
active participle of an imaginary denominative from H3754 (כֶּרֶם);
a vinedresser
KJV: vine dresser (as one or two words).

H3756.definition:
from H3754 (כֶּרֶם); gardener;
Karmi, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Carmi.

H3757.definition:
patronymically from H3756 (כַּרְמִי);
a Karmite or descendant of Karmi
KJV: Carmites.

H3758.definition:
probably of foreign origin;
carmine, a deep red
KJV: crimson.

H3759.definition:
from H3754 (כֶּרֶם);
a planted field (garden, orchard, vineyard or park); by implication, garden produce
KJV: full (green) ears (of corn), fruitful field (place), plentiful (field).

H3760.definition:
the same as H3759 (כַּרְמֶל);
Karmel, the name of a hill and of a town in Palestine
KJV: Carmel, fruitful (plentiful) field, (place).

H3761.definition:
patron from H3760 (כַּרְמֶל);
a Karmelite or inhabitant of Karmel (the town)
KJV: Carmelite.

H3762.definition:
feminine of H3761 (כַּרְמְלִי);
a Karmelitess or female inhabitant of Karmel
KJV: Carmelitess.

H3763.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Keran, an aboriginal Idumaean
KJV: Cheran.

H3764.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3678 (כִּסֵּא);
a throne
KJV: throne.

H3765.definition:
from H3697 (כָּסַם);
to lay waste
KJV: waste.

H3766.definition:
a primitive root;
to bend the knee; by implication, to sink, to prostrate
KJV: bow (down, self), bring down (low), cast down, couch, fall, feeble, kneeling, sink, smite (stoop) down, subdue, [idiom] very.

H3767.definition:
from H3766 (כָּרַע);
the leg (from the knee to the ankle) of men or locusts (only in the dual)
KJV: leg.

H3768.definition:
of foreign origin;
byssus or fine vegetable wool
KJV: green.

H3769.definition:
a primitive root;
to dance (i.e. whirl)
KJV: dance(-ing).

H3770.definition:
by variation from H7164 (קָרַס);
the paunch or belly (as swelling out)
KJV: belly.

H3771.definition:
of foreign origin;
Karshena, a courtier of Xerxes
KJV: Carshena.

H3772.definition:
a primitive root;
to cut (off, down or asunder); by implication, to destroy or consume; specifically, to covenant (i.e. make an alliance or bargain, originally by cutting flesh and passing between the pieces)
KJV: be chewed, be con-(feder-) ate, covenant, cut (down, off), destroy, fail, feller, be freed, hew (down), make a league (covenant), [idiom] lose, perish, [idiom] utterly, [idiom] want.

H3773.definition:
passive participle feminine of H3772 (כָּרַת);
something cut, i.e. a hewn timber
KJV: beam.

H3775.definition:
apparently by transposition for H3532 (כֶּבֶשׂ);
a young sheep
KJV: lamb.

H3776.definition:
feminine of H3775 (כֶּשֶׂב);
a young ewe
KJV: lamb.

H3777.definition:
from an unused root of uncertain meaning;
Kesed, a relative of Abraham
KJV: Chesed.

H3778.definition:
(occasionally with enclitic) כַּשְׂדִּימָה; towards the Kasdites into Chaldea), patronymically from H3777 (כֶּשֶׂד) (only in the plural);
a Kasdite, or descendant of Kesed; by implication, a Chaldaean (as if so descended); also an astrologer (as if proverbial of that people
KJV: Chaldeans, Chaldees, inhabitants of Chaldea.

H3779.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3778 (כַּשְׂדִּי);
a Chaldaean or inhabitant of Chaldaea; by implication, a Magian or professional astrologer
KJV: Chaldean.

H3780.definition:
a primitive root;
to grow fat (i.e. be covered with flesh)
KJV: be covered. Compare H3680 (כָּסָה).

H3781.definition:
from H3782 (כָּשַׁל);
properly, a feller, i.e. an axe
KJV: ax.

H3782.definition:
a primitive root;
to totter or waver (through weakness of the legs, especially the ankle); by implication, to falter, stumble, faint or fall
KJV: bereave (from the margin), cast down, be decayed, (cause to) fail, (cause, make to) fall (down, -ing), feeble, be (the) ruin(-ed, of), (be) overthrown, (cause to) stumble, [idiom] utterly, be weak.

H3783.definition:
from H3782 (כָּשַׁל);
properly, a tottering, i.e. ruin
KJV: fall.

H3784.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to whisper aspell, i.e. to inchant or practise magic
KJV: sorcerer, (use) witch(-craft).

H3785.definition:
from H3784 (כָּשַׁף);
magic
KJV: sorcery, witchcraft.

H3786.definition:
from H3784 (כָּשַׁף);
a magician
KJV: sorcerer.

H3787.definition:
a primitive root properly, to be straight or right;
by implication, to be acceptable; also to succeed or prosper
KJV: direct, be right, prosper.

H3788.definition:
from H3787 (כָּשֵׁר);
success, advantage
KJV: equity, good, right.

H3789.definition:
a primitive root;
to grave, by implication, to write (describe, inscribe, prescribe, subscribe)
KJV: describe, record, prescribe, subscribe, write(-ing, -ten).

H3790.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3789 (כָּתַב)
{to grave, by implication, to write (describe, inscribe, prescribe, subscribe)}
KJV: write(-ten).

H3791.definition:
from H3789 (כָּתַב);
something written, i.e. a writing, record or book
KJV: register, scripture, writing.

H3792.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3791 (כָּתָב)
{something written, i.e. a writing, record or book}
KJV: prescribing, writing(-ten).

H3793.definition:
from H3789 (כָּתַב);
a letter or other mark branded on the skin
KJV: [idiom] any (mark).

H3794.definition:
or כִּתִּיִּי; patrial from an unused name denoting Cyprus (only in the plural);
a Kittite or Cypriote; hence, an islander in general, i.e. the Greeks or Romans on the shores opposite Palestine
KJV: Chittim, Kittim.

H3795.definition:
from H3807 (כָּתַת);
beaten, i.e. pure (oil)
KJV: beaten.

H3796.definition:
from an unused root meaning to compact;
a wall (as gathering inmates)
KJV: wall.

H3797.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3796 (כֹּתֶל)
{a wall (as gathering inmates)}
KJV: wall.

H3798.definition:
from H3796 (כֹּתֶל) and H376 (אִישׁ); wall of a man;
Kithlish, a place in Palestine
KJV: Kithlish.

H3799.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to carve or engrave, i.e. (by implication) to inscribe indelibly
KJV: mark.
